# Project styling — Tailwind only

This portfolio uses **Tailwind CSS v4** (`@import "tailwindcss"` + `@theme inline` in `app/globals.css`).

## Do

- Put presentation on `className` with Tailwind utilities.
- Use semantic tokens: `text-ink`, `text-body`, `bg-ink`, `bg-paper`, `border-ink`, `font-display`, `font-body`.
- Prefer mobile-first responsive utilities (`md:`, `lg:`).
- Follow `docs/rules/project-rules.md` for full project law.

## Do not

- Do **not** add `<style>{\`...\`}</style>` (or styled-jsx) inside React components.
- Do **not** duplicate the same rules in both Tailwind and a component style tag.

## Exceptions

Only in `app/globals.css`, as named classes: keyframes, sibling/complex selectors, container-query type (`cqi`), paper grain, scroll-snap bands. Reference those class names from JSX; never inline the CSS in the component.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<section>
  <style>{`.foo { margin: 32px; }`}</style>
</section>

// ✅ GOOD
<section className="mx-8 border-y border-ink py-8">
```
